{"id":"dfeea176-d17a-4414-a4f2-6ab5b5064859","object":"chat.completion","created":1785024458,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\": \"import math\\n\\ndef solve(case):\\n    matrix = case['matrix']\\n    if not matrix or not matrix[0]:\\n        raise ValueError('Empty matrix')\\n    n = len(matrix)\\n    m = len(matrix[0])\\n    for row in matrix:\\n        if len(row) != m:\\n            raise ValueError('Inconsistent row lengths')\\n    # document frequency per column\\n    df = [0] * m\\n    for i in range(n):\\n        for j in range(m):\\n            if matrix[i][j] != 0:\\n                df[j] += 1\\n    # compute IDF\\n    idf = []\\n    for j in range(m):\\n        val = math.log(1 + n / (1 + df[j]))\\n        idf.append(round(val, 6))\\n    # weighted matrix and row degree\\n    weighted_matrix = []\\n    row_degree = []\\n    for i in range(n):\\n        row = matrix[i]\\n        wrow = []\\n        s = 0.0\\n        for j in range(m):\\n            w = row[j] * idf[j]\\n            rw = round(w, 6)\\n            wrow.append(rw)\\n            s += rw\\n        weighted_matrix.append(wrow)\\n        row_degree.append(round(s, 6))\\n    return {'idf': idf, 'row_degree': row_degree, 'weighted_matrix': weighted_matrix}\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to write a solve(case) function in Python. The case payload has a \"matrix\" field which is a list of lists (binary? looks like 0/1). The task is to compute IDF, weighted matrix, and row degrees. Based on the description: compute IDF per feature (column) as log(1 + number_of_rows / (1 + document_frequency)). Document frequency = number of rows where the feature (column) is nonzero. Then multiply each entry in matrix by its feature IDF to get weighted_matrix. Then row_degree is sum over columns for each row of the weighted matrix. Also for idf output: array of IDF values for features (columns). self_similarity_removed? Not sure if that means we should remove self-similarity (diagonal?) but matrix doesn't have diagonal. Probably just compute as described. Output must have \"idf\", \"row_degree\", \"weighted_matrix\". Validate nonempty rectangular matrix. Use math.log for natural log? The description says log(1 + N/(1+df)). Typically IDF uses log base 2 or natural? Not specified. Usually in NLP it's log base 10 or natural. But given that it's \"log\" without base, likely natural log. Use math.log (natural). Also numeric_tolerance: round? It says \"Round and return IDF, weighted matrix, and row degrees.\" So we need to round to some precision? Not specified. Possibly round to 6 decimal places? Or maybe round to nearest integer? The example outputs not given. The output schema says type=number. So presumably floats. We'll round to 6 decimal places or keep as floats. But they said \"Round and return IDF, weighted matrix, and row degrees.\" So maybe round to 3? Since no specification, we'll round to 6 decimals to be safe. Or maybe use Python's default rounding? The instruction: \"Round and return ...\" In the context of spectral preprocessing, they might want to round to avoid floating point errors. I'll use round(x, 6) for each number. Ensure weighted_matrix entries are rounded. row_degree rounded. idf rounded.\n\nWe need to output exactly the three fields. No _case_nonce in output.\n\nDo not mutate input. So deep copy? Actually we can just read values and create new lists.\n\nImplementation steps:\n1. Validate matrix: nonempty list, each row same length, all 0/1? But not required, could be any numeric. We'll assume numeric.\n2. N = number of rows, M = number of columns.\n3. Compute document frequency: for each column j, count rows i where matrix[i][j] != 0.\n4. Compute IDF: idf[j] = log(1 + N / (1 + df_j))  (natural log). Round each.\n5. Compute weighted matrix: for each row i, for each column j, weighted_matrix[i][j] = matrix[i][j] * idf[j]; then round.\n6. Compute row_degree: for each row i, sum(weighted_matrix[i][j]) over j; round.\n\nReturn dict with keys \"idf\", \"row_degree\", \"weighted_matrix\".\n\nWeighted matrix and row_degree rounded.\n\nEdge cases: df could be zero? then log(1 + N/1) = log(1+N). That's fine.\n\nRaise ValueError if invalid: e.g., empty matrix, rows of different lengths.\n\nNow produce the implementation code. Must be assigned to 'implementation' key as a JSON string. We'll write the Python code as a string, escape properly.\n\nI'll output:\n\n{\"implementation\": \"import math\\ndef solve(case):\\n    matrix = case['matrix']\\n    if not matrix or not matrix[0]:\\n        raise ValueError('Empty matrix')\\n    n = len(matrix)\\n    m = len(matrix[0])\\n    for row in matrix:\\n        if len(row) != m:\\n            raise ValueError('Inconsistent row lengths')\\n    # compute document frequency per column\\n    df = [0]*m\\n    for i in range(n):\\n        for j in range(m):\\n            if matrix[i][j] != 0:\\n                df[j] += 1\\n    # compute IDF\\n    idf = [0.0]*m\\n    import math\\n    for j in range(m):\\n        idf[j] = math.log(1 + n/(1 + df[j]))\\n        idf[j] = round(idf[j], 6)\\n    # compute weighted matrix and row degrees\\n    weighted_matrix = []\\n    row_degree = []\\n    for i in range(n):\\n        row = matrix[i]\\n        wrow = []\\n        sum_row = 0.0\\n        for j in range(m):\\n            val = row[j] * idf[j]\\n            rval = round(val, 6)\\n            wrow.append(rval)\\n            sum_row += rval\\n        weighted_matrix.append(wrow)\\n        row_degree.append(round(sum_row, 6))\\n    return {\\\"idf\\\": idf, \\\"row_degree\\\": row_degree, \\\"weighted_matrix\\\": weighted_matrix}\"}\n\nMake sure to escape quotes and newlines properly. We'll write as a JSON string.\n\nNote: The schema requires \"idf\" array of numbers, \"row_degree\" array of numbers, \"weighted_matrix\" array of arrays of numbers. Our output matches.\n\nAlso note that the task says \"self_similarity_removed\" but the matrix has no meaning of self-similarity; we ignore.\n\nNow produce final answer."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1417,"completion_tokens":1552,"total_tokens":2969,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1408},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1209},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1408,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":9},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}